Utilize React.lazy and Suspense for code-splitting and better performance
Implement proper error boundaries to handle and display errors gracefully
Use PropTypes or TypeScript for type checking and better code maintainability

OpenAI Best Practices:

Implement proper error handling and retries for API requests
Use streaming responses for large language model outputs to improve user experience
Implement rate limiting and proper API key management for security
Cache API responses where appropriate to reduce costs and improve performance
Use the latest model versions for better results and security updates
Implement proper input sanitization to prevent prompt injection attacks

AI SDK Best Practices:

Follow the SDK's documentation for proper initialization and usage
Implement proper error handling and logging for SDK operations
Use the SDK's built-in features for authentication and authorization
Regularly update the SDK to benefit from performance improvements and security patches
